L\/MXLTap\/color","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTap":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTap"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTap"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltap","role":"symbol","title":"MXLTap","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTap","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tap type indicates a tap on the fretboard. The text content allows specification of the notation; + and T"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are common choices. If the element is empty, the hand attribute is used to specify the symbol to use. The hand"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is ignored if the tap glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hand attribute are present, the display is application-specific."}]}}}